@tradition spice-shelf-supper
// Spice shelf supper (0.60.7): everyone brought one spice from home. Brennan cooks Tuesday dinner with three of them,
// and the jars line a shelf by the servery that grows over the weeks (the deck architect's spice shelf, always there).
// A meal tradition: going to it IS dinner for those who go.
k: 443
title: Spice shelf supper
when: weekly tuesday
at: 18:15-19:15
min: 25
where: 3 room Mess hall: mess-seat
hold: none
who: brennan always, lingers-at-meals 70%, galley 60%, everyone 40%
anim: talk
host: brennan
from: brennan
ties: galley meal=dinner
meal: dinner

== mail
- Spice shelf supper tomorrow at dinner, from {time}. Three jars off the shelf this week. Guess whose they are.

== ask
- Spice shelf supper tonight. I hope she picks my jar.   #warm
- Brennan's cooking from the spice shelf. Bring an appetite and a glass of water.   #funny
- Supper from the spice shelf at quarter past six. Three jars, three homes.   #warm

== here
- That's my gran's pepper. I'd know it anywhere.   #warm
- Whose is the smoky one? I need to know.
- Too hot. Wonderful. Too hot.   #funny

== thanks
- You eat from Brennan's spice shelf supper. Somebody tells you whose spice is in it, and where it came from.   #warm

== chatter
- The spice shelf's three jars longer than last month.
- One day I'll find out whose jar is the green one.   #funny
- Every jar on that shelf came a long way.   #warm
